{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_a140385fa8cf4bcf8b7710a78b403996","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tasks complete. Final delivery statement:\n\n## Delivery\n\nI inspected the restored source-only build, found the two flagged self-inflicted gaps, observed the corresponding public reference behavior with ordinary browser tools, and repaired my own implementation.\n\n**Issues fixed**\n1. **SearchPage no-op form.** `MorePages.tsx` SearchPage called `e.preventDefault()` with no effect. Observed the reference: submitting (Enter or the submit control) navigates to `/search/?keywords=<query>` and re-renders the same search form (no offline result list, input not re-prefilled). Rewrote SearchPage to submit through the router to `/search/?keywords=<encoded>`, preserving the observed accessible structure (`search` → `list` → `listitem` → label \"Keywords\" + textbox) and the inline magnifier submit control.\n2. **Missing `/about/privacy-statement/` route.** PrivacyPage linked to it but `App.routeFor` fell through to home. Observed the reference page (\"Privacy Statement › Corravale University\"), including its two collapsible \"Special Notices\" disclosures and the exact `#coppa`/`#eu` anchors targeted by the Privacy Notice page. Implemented `src/pages/PrivacyStatementPage.tsx` (title band, prose body, Overview/Scope/Categories/Use/Access/Security/Changes/Contact sections, COPPA + EU-GDPR disclosure content), registered the route + document title, and added its per-route header chrome (report label \"Report Sexual Misconduct, Discrimination or Harassment\", Quick Links with \"Learn\").\n\n**Public-behavior checks completed** (reference action → observed → candidate parity, recorded in `public_behavior_checklist.md`): header Quick Links open/close (desktop + mobile, per-route labels), header search Enter/button → `/search/?keywords=`, search-page Enter/button submission, footer links (Privacy Notice `/about/privacy/`, Contact us `/contact/`, `tel:` phone, campuses, `/_404.html` destinations), main nav + audiences, expandable About sidebar rosters (`aria-expanded`), the privacy-notice → privacy-statement link, `#coppa`/`#eu` anchor navigation + scroll + disclosure toggle, the `/_404.html` offline notice, and direct-route/reload/back navigation.\n\n**Verification**: built with `npm install && npm run build` (Vite + React 19 + Tailwind 4 + TS), copied `dist/index.html` → `output/index.html` (md5 identical, single self-contained file). Tested that exact file over a preview server at desktop 1920×1080 and mobile 375×812 — client-side routing, anchors, search submission, and Quick Links all functional, with **0 console errors** across interactions."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1053951,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1eaa6c29-60a4-48e2-abd6-c10828342ccd","uuid":"cb229c57-c61a-4bd4-ae2e-f7cab6a13f5a"}
